From 82ce52e2a621c494f267e24e09fdb09bb592de29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:05:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] krans: decoder runs with the states in registers per
 shape, cold set-up code; build lists

The decoder's unchecked runs are instantiated for the shapes the encoder writes (order 0, order 1,
four neighbours, four neighbouring words; eight states) and one general call; segment starts and
the end of the word stream take one checked routine. Object text 61.0 KB -> 29.0 KB at
-O3 -march=native (stripped build/kolmo: 3,500,808 -> 3,533,576 bytes against rc3).
krans.c needs libm (the encoder's table choice), so it is listed on its own (KRSRC) and not in
NATSRC, whose tests link without it; the Python and Rust bindings' source lists get the file
(not built here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
